{c: Intro}
[G]  [G]   [C]  [G]
[D]  [Em]  [C]  [D]

{c: Verse 1}
What [G]love could remember no [C]wrongs we have [G]done
Om[D]niscient, all [Em]knowing, he [C]counts not their [D]sum
Thrown [G]into a [Am]sea without [G/B]bottom or s[C]hore
[G/B]Our [C2]sins they are [G/D]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: Chorus}
[G]Praise the [C]Lo[G]rd[Em]
His [D]mercy is [C]mo[G]re[D]
[C]Stronger than [G]darkness, [D/F#]new every m[Em7]orn
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: Verse 2}
What [G]patience would wait as we [C]constantly [G]roam
What [D]father, so [Em]tender, is [C]calling us [D]home
He [G]welcomes the [Am]weakest, the [G/B]vilest, the [C]poor
[G/B]Our [C2]sins they are [G/D]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: Chorus}
[G]Praise the [C]Lo[G]rd[Em]
His [D]mercy is [C]mo[G]re[D]
[C]Stronger than [G]darkness, [D/F#]new every m[Em7]orn
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: Instrumental}

{c: Verse 3}
What [G]riches of kindness he [C]lavished on [G]us
His [D]blood was the [Em]payment, his [C]life was the [D]cost
We [G]stood 'neath a [Am]debt we could [G/B]never af[C]ford
[G/B]Our [C2]sins they are [G/D]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: Chorus}
[G]Praise the [C]Lo[G]rd[Em]
His [D]mercy is [C]mo[G]re[D]
[C]Stronger than [G]darkness, [D/F#]new every m[Em7]orn
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: DRUM SOLO, INST CUT}
[G]Praise the [C]Lo[G]rd[Em]
His [D]mercy is [C]mo[G]re[D]
[C]Stronger than [G]darkness, [D/F#]new every m[Em7]orn
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more

{c: ALL IN. REPEAT LAST LINE X1}
Praise the [C]Lo[G]rd[Em]
His [D]mercy is [C]mo[G]re[D]
[C]Stronger than [G]darkness, [D/F#]new every m[Em7]orn
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [Em]more
Our [C]sins they are [G]many, his [D]mercy is [G]more
